# Usage stats

Settings section `usage-stats` is the desktop restyle of `dsh-usage-panel`. Tokens / `ui-primitives` only; billing = ESTIMATE (peak/valley buckets × user prices, official price table asOf 2026-08-17 with source link); no `/user/balance`, no balance APIs. Unpriced models show "set a price"/em dash, never a guessed figure (competitor red line stands). Peak/valley windows: Beijing UTC+8 Monday–Friday 09:00–12:00 & 14:00–18:00; a step bills at its step/start instant; compaction never enters cost buckets. UTC day buckets in v1. Desktop `desktop-plugins` copy wins over a marketplace install of the same package. Empty state is no billed usage (blank-only sessions included) with no scan failures; light heatmap empty cells must stay visible. Mounting rides the desktop overlay `desktop-usage-panel.patch.yml` (`--patch`, full starts only) — never a managed block in the user-owned `cordis.patch.yml`; the overlay is deleted when disabled, ensure fails, or a marketplace bundle already mounts the package. The plugin client registers ONLY `settings.section` — never a `conversation.composer.dock` entry: the peak/valley status + session-cost row under the composer belongs to the harness `PeakValleyRow` (session-cost-display card), and a plugin-side strip duplicated that line after the pr-76/pr-79 merge (removed 2026-09-02).

